<title>SRI LANKA: Cold Stores slips on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Cold Stores slips on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ceylon Cold Stores Ltd dropped sharply on Thursday by 5.3 pct or ten rupees to 180 on retail profit-taking, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Retail investors are taking profits after the high gains made by the share,&quot; said Alastair Corera of Forbes &amp; Walker Stock Brokers.</p>
<p>Cold Stores produces and markets frozen foods and bottled drinks and is a subsidiary of John Keells Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>--- Colombo newsroom (941)434319</p>
